conference:
  name: "The 3rd International Conference on Advances in Machine Intelligence and Cybersecurity Technologies (AMICT 2026)"
  location: "Labuan, Malaysia"
  start: 2026-11-12
  end: 2026-11-13
year: 2026
abstract: >-
  Automated anemia screening from peripheral blood smears is attractive because
  red-blood-cell morphology carries diagnostic signal, yet existing work on the
  AneRBC dataset relies on unimodal CNN classifiers, an unpublished train/test
  split, and discards the free-text CBC and morphology reports paired with every
  image. We build a reproducible benchmark (fixed stratified 5-fold split plus a
  multi-task label set mined from the paired reports) and introduce HemaFormer, a
  report-supervised multi-task network. From the image alone at inference it
  matches strong pretrained baselines on anemia classification while additionally
  predicting morphology background, poikilocyte features and CBC indices. With
  bootstrap confidence intervals we report calibrated negative results: neither
  contrastive report grounding nor auxiliary multi-task supervision significantly
  improves the near-saturated anemia metric at this data scale.
keywords:
  - anemia
  - peripheral blood smear
  - multi-task learning
  - report supervision
  - AneRBC
  - reproducibility
